₹1,000 assigned against a ₹700 target read "Over-funded ₹700 of ₹700":
the target line worked its figure back from what was still missing, which
can never exceed the target. Past the target it now shows what was
actually assigned (₹1,000 of ₹700); the bar still stops full.

An overspend covered back to ₹0 (₹700 assigned, ₹900 spent, ₹200 moved
in) read "Over-funded", because more had been assigned than the target
asked. The extra went to the spending, so nothing is spare: the label is
now "Over-funded" only while the balance is above zero, "Funded" otherwise.
The engine's funded state is unchanged; this is the screen's word for it.

Tests: over-funded-label.test.ts renders both envelopes on the budget.

